                520
              ]
            }
          ],
          "orig": "This document exercises a list that switches type across nesting depth: an ordered list containing a nested unordered list, and (further down) an unordered list containing a nested ordered list. The plain lists.html fixture already nests same-type lists (ul-in-ul, ol-in-ol) and flattens them into a single group with only the bullet/number marker changing per item; this fixture checks whether a type switch across the nesting boundary changes that behavior - e.g. produces a separate child group, or a different label.",
          "text": "This document exercises a list that switches type across nesting depth: an ordered list containing a nested unordered list, and (further down) an unordered list containing a nested ordered list. The plain lists.html fixture already nests same-type lists (ul-in-ul, ol-in-ol) and flattens them into a single group with only the bullet/number marker changing per item; this fixture checks whether a type switch across the nesting boundary changes that behavior - e.g. produces a separate child group, or a different label.",
          "formatting": null,
